Prevent tiny constants from retaining idle image-sized Vulkan buffers.

Co-created with GPT (OpenAI), 2026-11-08.
The previous 64 MiB reuse slack could assign a 16 MiB image plane to a
12-byte constant. For requests below 64 KiB, cap pool capacity at twice
the request or 4 KiB, whichever is larger. Leave larger image allocation
reuse unchanged. This changes storage policy, not shader arithmetic.

